  <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px;">
    <div class="panel" style="border-left: 3px solid var(--green);">
      <h3 style="color: var(--green); margin: 0 0 8px 0; font-size: 15px;">
        Why is CloseMeet Lite capped at 6 participants per room?
      </h3>
      <p class="muted" style="font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.7; margin: 0;">
        CloseMeet Lite uses a serverless Full-Mesh P2P topology where every participant connects directly to every other participant ($N(N-1)/2$ connections). At 6 participants, the mesh maintains 15 bidirectional P2P links within a strict &lt;15% CPU and 4.5 Mbps uplink budget. A 7th participant attempt is atomically rejected (<code class="code">ROOM_FULL</code>) at both the signaling and client layers to guarantee zero frame drops without a central SFU server.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="panel" style="border-left: 3px solid var(--green);">
      <h3 style="color: var(--green); margin: 0 0 8px 0; font-size: 15px;">
        How does the Fail-Closed E2EE architecture protect media and files?
      </h3>
      <p class="muted" style="font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.7; margin: 0;">
        Session keys are derived locally using RFC 5869 HKDF-SHA256 from a 256-bit session secret and optional room password. Every media frame and 64 KB file chunk is encrypted via Windows CNG (<code class="code">bcrypt.lib</code>) AES-256-GCM with a unique 96-bit monotonic IV and 128-bit authentication tag. Any packet that fails authentication tag verification is discarded immediately before reaching decoder or UI buffers.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="panel" style="border-left: 3px solid var(--green);">
      <h3 style="color: var(--green); margin: 0 0 8px 0; font-size: 15px;">
        Does CloseMeet Lite require port forwarding or administrator privileges?
      </h3>
      <p class="muted" style="font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.7; margin: 0;">
        Neither. CloseMeet Lite opens 0 inbound listening sockets on Windows Defender Firewall, relying strictly on outbound WebRTC ICE UDP hole-punching (or optional TURN Privacy Relay for IP masking). Furthermore, the Inno Setup installer runs with <code class="code">PrivilegesRequired=lowest</code> (<code class="code">asInvoker</code>), installing cleanly to user space without UAC elevation.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
